      "hints": [
        "Each page has its own <b>Save changes</b> button.",
        "WEP and WPA/TKIP are broken; WPA3 (SAE) is the current standard.",
        "WPS PINs can be brute-forced, and UPnP lets devices open ports without you knowing."
      ],
      "solution": "<p>Wireless: WPA3-Personal, a long passphrase, WPS off. Guest: on, isolation on, WPA2/WPA3. Administration: a new 12+ character password, remote management off, UPnP off, auto-update on. Port forwarding: delete the port 23 rule; add TCP 443 → 192.168.0.40:443.</p>",
      "review": "<p>These are the SOHO hardening steps Network+ expects: strong wireless encryption, no WPS, changed default credentials, minimal exposed services, updated firmware, and guest isolation.</p>"
    }
